{
  "identifier": "colorjs-color-space",
  "name": "color-space",
  "version": "3.4.0",
  "description": "Color conversions math for 221+ color spaces, including OKLCH, CIELAB, CAM16, HCT, Display P3, Rec. 2020, camera logs, print and appearance models. Every space is tested against a cited reference value. A color goes in as any CSS string or as channel values. Tools: convert, gamut, css, space, spaces, cube, shader, icc and code. No API key, no configuration and no network.",
  "author": "Dmitry Ivanov",
  "authorUrl": "https://github.com/dy",
  "homepage": "https://color-space.io/",
  "icon": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/colorjs/color-space/master/web/img/locus-400.png",
  "category": "developer",
  "tags": [
    "color",
    "color-space",
    "color-conversion",
    "color-science",
    "oklch",
    "oklab",
    "cielab",
    "cam16",
    "css-color",
    "wide-gamut",
    "hdr",
    "shader",
    "lut",
    "icc"
  ],
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "convert",
      "title": "Convert color",
      "description": "Convert a color between any two of the 221 color spaces, identity included, in each space's conventional ranges (rgb 0-255, oklch L 0-1 / C 0-0.4 / H 0-360, lab L 0-100 …). The color goes in as a CSS string (`color`) or as channel values (`from` + `values`); a batch as `colors` – tuples in `from`, CSS strings, or both. Out-of-range in, unclamped out: `inRange` flags each channel against the target's conventional range (rgb below 0 means outside sRGB); null = undefined at that coordinate.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "from": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "source space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          },
          "to": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "target space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          },
          "values": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "number"
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "maxItems": 4,
            "description": "one color in the source space, e.g. [255, 128, 0] for rgb"
          },
          "color": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "a CSS color instead of `from` + `values`: '#ff8000', 'rebeccapurple', 'oklch(0.7 0.1 50)', 'lab(54% 80 67)', 'color(display-p3 1 0.5 0)'"
          },
          "colors": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "number"
                  },
                  "minItems": 1,
                  "maxItems": 4
                },
                {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "maxItems": 1024,
            "description": "a batch: one tuple (in `from`) or CSS string per color, e.g. [[255, 128, 0], '#00ff80', 'oklch(0.7 0.1 50)']"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "to"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "from": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "to": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "channels": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "symbol",
                "name",
                "min",
                "max"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "symbol": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "name": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "min": {
                  "type": "number"
                },
                "max": {
                  "type": "number"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "colors": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "from",
                "values",
                "inRange"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "from": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "values": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": [
                      "number",
                      "null"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                "inRange": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "boolean"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "to",
          "channels",
          "colors"
        ]
      },
      "annotations": {
        "title": "Convert color",
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "gamut",
      "title": "Gamut membership",
      "description": "Which standard display gamuts hold a color — sRGB ⊂ Display P3 ⊂ Rec. 2020, each tested in its own RGB box straight from the source space, the same ladder as the color-space.io gamut pill. `smallest` is the tightest one; null = beyond Rec. 2020. Membership only: nothing is gamut-mapped.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "from": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "source space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          },
          "values": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "number"
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "maxItems": 4,
            "description": "one color in the source space"
          },
          "color": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "a CSS color instead of `from` + `values`: '#ff8000', 'rebeccapurple', 'oklch(0.7 0.1 50)', 'lab(54% 80 67)', 'color(display-p3 1 0.5 0)'"
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "smallest": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ],
            "enum": [
              "srgb",
              "display-p3",
              "rec2020",
              null
            ]
          },
          "gamuts": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "gamut",
                "space",
                "inside",
                "values"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "gamut": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "space": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "white": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "primaries": {
                  "type": "object"
                },
                "inside": {
                  "type": "boolean"
                },
                "values": {
                  "anyOf": [
                    {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "type": [
                          "number",
                          "null"
                        ]
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "null"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "smallest",
          "gamuts"
        ]
      },
      "annotations": {
        "title": "Gamut membership",
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "css",
      "title": "CSS color strings",
      "description": "A color as CSS Color 4 strings — rgb(), hsl(), hwb(), lab(), lch(), oklab(), oklch() and color(display-p3 | a98-rgb | prophoto-rgb | srgb-linear | xyz-d65 | xyz-d50) — plus #hex inside sRGB. Converted, never gamut-mapped: a string is null where CSS would clamp it into a different color (rgb/hsl/hwb outside sRGB, lightness out of range). `gamut` is the smallest display gamut that holds the color.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "from": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "source space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          },
          "values": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "number"
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "maxItems": 4,
            "description": "one color in the source space"
          },
          "color": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "a CSS color instead of `from` + `values`: '#ff8000', 'rebeccapurple', 'oklch(0.7 0.1 50)', 'lab(54% 80 67)', 'color(display-p3 1 0.5 0)'"
          },
          "notations": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "rgb",
                "hsl",
                "hwb",
                "lab",
                "lchab",
                "oklab",
                "oklch",
                "p3",
                "a98rgb",
                "prophoto",
                "xyz",
                "xyz-d50",
                "lrgb"
              ]
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "description": "only these, by library space id (default: all)"
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "hex": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "gamut": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "css": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "space",
                "css"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "space": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "css": {
                  "type": [
                    "string",
                    "null"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "hex",
          "gamut",
          "css"
        ]
      },
      "annotations": {
        "title": "CSS color strings",
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "space",
      "title": "Space dossier",
      "description": "The dossier of one color space: display name (as color-space.io shows it), description, channels + conventional ranges, defining references, provenance (year, author), illuminant/observer, encoding class, family and purpose, and its direct conversion neighbours.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "the space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "name"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "family": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "purpose": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "channels": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "symbol",
                "name",
                "min",
                "max"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "symbol": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "name": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "min": {
                  "type": "number"
                },
                "max": {
                  "type": "number"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "neighbors": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "source": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "name",
          "title",
          "family",
          "purpose",
          "channels",
          "neighbors",
          "source"
        ]
      },
      "annotations": {
        "title": "Space dossier",
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "spaces",
      "title": "Space catalog",
      "description": "List the 221 color spaces with display name, family, purpose, channels and one-line use. Optional filters: `query` (words matched against id, name, use line and description; best matches first), `family`, `purpose`.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "query": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "free text, e.g. 'camera log', 'cielab', 'display p3'"
          },
          "family": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "Display & web",
              "RGB remixes",
              "Perceptual",
              "Colorimetry & research",
              "Video & broadcast",
              "Film & camera",
              "Print & paint"
            ]
          },
          "purpose": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "picking",
              "palettes",
              "editing",
              "compositing",
              "grading",
              "delivery",
              "print",
              "difference",
              "measurement",
              "research"
            ]
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "count": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "spaces": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "name",
                "title",
                "family",
                "purpose",
                "channels"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "name": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "title": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "family": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "purpose": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string"
                  }
                },
                "channels": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "use": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "count",
          "spaces"
        ]
      },
      "annotations": {
        "title": "Space catalog",
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "cube",
      "title": ".cube LUT",
      "description": "Render a conversion as a .cube LUT file (Resolve, Premiere, Final Cut, OBS, ffmpeg). The header carries the measured deviation vs the direct conversion. Pure per-channel transfers auto-emit 1D. Size ≤ 33 here (larger via the library or https://color-space.io/).",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "from": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "source space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          },
          "to": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "target space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          },
          "size": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 2,
            "maximum": 33,
            "description": "3D lattice size (default 17)"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "from",
          "to"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "annotations": {
        "title": ".cube LUT",
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "shader",
      "title": "Shader code",
      "description": "The conversion as shader source – GLSL (WebGL2; WebGL1 too unless the path reads a table), WGSL (WebGPU), HLSL (DirectX, Unity, Unreal) or MSL (Metal) – with an entry function `<from>_<to>` (hyphens stripped), e.g. `vec3 rgb_oklch(vec3 c)`, plus every function on the path. Each language is differentially tested against the library and compiled on real GPUs: use it instead of writing color matrices. HLSL and MSL need the optional peer `naga-wasm` installed beside color-space.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "from": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "source space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          },
          "to": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "target space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          },
          "language": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "glsl",
              "wgsl",
              "hlsl",
              "msl"
            ],
            "description": "default glsl"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "from",
          "to"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "language": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "entry": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "code": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "language",
          "entry",
          "code"
        ]
      },
      "annotations": {
        "title": "Shader code",
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "icc",
      "title": "ICC profile",
      "description": "One space as an ICC v2 profile (.icc): matrix + tone curve where the space is an RGB working space (Photoshop, OS color management), a CLUT on a Lab PCS otherwise (lcms, ArgyllCMS, ImageMagick). Returned as a base64 embedded resource; `class`, `pcs` and `bytes` describe it.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "the space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          },
          "grid": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 2,
            "maximum": 65,
            "description": "CLUT lattice points per channel, CLUT profiles only (default 33 for 3 channels; fewer = a smaller file)"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "name"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "file": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "class": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "pcs": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "bytes": {
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "name",
          "file",
          "class",
          "pcs",
          "bytes"
        ]
      },
      "annotations": {
        "title": "ICC profile",
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "code",
      "title": "Library code",
      "description": "The conversion as code to paste: the color-space JS call with its result and – where one exists for the space on the non-sRGB side – the colour-science (Python) equivalent verified against color-space (sRGB ↔ that space), with any named caveat. The color goes in as a CSS string or as values in `from` (default: sRGB 200, 100, 50).",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "from": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "source space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          },
          "to": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "target space id, e.g. 'rgb', 'oklch', 'lab', 'slog3', 'rec709' (the 'spaces' tool lists all 221)"
          },
          "values": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "number"
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "maxItems": 4,
            "description": "the color in the source space"
          },
          "color": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "a CSS color instead of `from` + `values`: '#ff8000', 'rebeccapurple', 'oklch(0.7 0.1 50)', 'lab(54% 80 67)', 'color(display-p3 1 0.5 0)'"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "to"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "js": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "python": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "pythonFor": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "js",
          "python",
          "pythonFor"
        ]
      },
      "annotations": {
        "title": "Library code",
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false
      }
    }
  ],
  "resources": [
    {
      "name": "data.json",
